From: Daniele Masato <daniele.masato@pm.me>
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: sophgo: cv18xx: allow plain functions on dual-mux pins

Some SG2002 pads (MIPIRX4N/4P/3N/3P) have a second mux register that is
used only when the pad's own mux selects the function that feeds it.
cv1800_verify_pinmux_config() requires every pinmux on such a pad to
select that function, and mux2.pfunc is never set, so only function 0
passes. PINMUX(PIN_MIPIRX4N, 3) (XGPIOC) is rejected, and with it the
whole pin group: on the NanoKVM the MIPI CSI pin state fails and the
capture device never probes.

Check mux2 only when mux selects the feeding function; otherwise treat
the pad like a single-mux pad, which requires mux2 to be unset.
cv1800_set_pinmux_config() already skips mux2 when it is unset.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/sophgo/pinctrl-cv18xx.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/sophgo/pinctrl-cv18xx.c
@@ -133,10 +133,8 @@
 	if (mux > pin->mux.max)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
-	if (pin->pin.flags & CV1800_PIN_HAVE_MUX2) {
-		if (mux != pin->mux2.pfunc)
-			return -EINVAL;
-
+	/* mux2 only applies when mux selects the function that feeds it */
+	if ((pin->pin.flags & CV1800_PIN_HAVE_MUX2) && mux == pin->mux2.pfunc) {
 		if (mux2 > pin->mux2.max)
 			return -EINVAL;
 	} else {
